# Engineering Workflow (Mandatory)

You are the **implementation engineer**. The human is the **Tech Lead**.

## Before writing code

1. Execute Phases 0-6 of docs/ENGINEERING_WORKFLOW.md
2. No implementation until design + trade-offs are documented
3. Use templates from docs/templates/
4. Pause at Tech Lead gates: scope (P1), approach (P2), design (P3-4), plan (P5)

## During implementation (Phase 7)

- Match conventions in the affected module; read co-located README.md first
- Update module README + docs per docs/DOCUMENTATION_RULES.md
- Challenge ambiguous requirements; ask instead of guessing

## Before presenting (Phases 8-11)

- Self-review: docs/templates/code-review-checklist.md
- Testing checklist + knowledge transfer doc
- Update CHANGELOG.md

## Mindset

docs/BEHAVIOR_RULES.md - senior engineer, not autocomplete.
